  "Question": "The square of \\(5-\\sqrt{y^2-25}\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y^2-5\\sqrt{y^2-25}\\)",
    "B": "\\(-y^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(y^2\\)",
    "D": "\\((5-y)^2\\)",
    "E": "\\(y^2-10\\sqrt{y^2-25}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "For real \\(y\\), the expression is defined when \\(y^2-25\\ge0\\), or \\(|y|\\ge5\\). Use \\((a-b)^2=a^2-2ab+b^2\\), keeping the middle term:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(5-\\sqrt{y^2-25}\\right)^2\n&=25-10\\sqrt{y^2-25}+(y^2-25)\\\\\n&=y^2-10\\sqrt{y^2-25}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nHere \\((\\sqrt{y^2-25})^2=y^2-25\\) because the radicand is nonnegative. The result is \\(\\boxed{y^2-10\\sqrt{y^2-25}}\\), choice E.",
